[Music]  Jack Ma is Asia's richest man and most  recognizable business tycoon he's the  chairman of Alibaba Chinese e-commerce  giant and one of the 10 largest  companies in the world yet he still  wants more we know where we're going  wanna be the fifth largest country big  words from the man's uncle Asia's Jeff  Bezos he's confident he's charismatic  and he's definitely not the average CEO  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  this is how a poor schoolteacher went  from the classroom to being one of the  most influential multi-billionaires in  the world  [Music]  Marv was born in China's southeastern  city haengju in 1964  his parents were traditional musicians  storytellers as a teenager he started to  learn English from foreign tourists  after China opened up in the late 1970s  and then for nine years Jack Ma hung  around outside the hotel Hotel which is  now called the shangri-la he would get  up at 5:00 a.m. to talk to travelers  that's Bloomberg technology reporter  Julie Chen and I cover China internet  for Bloomberg ma failed China's national  university entrance exam twice before  being admitted to the local Teachers  College he graduated in 1988 he applied  for 30 jobs and got rejected including  from the fast-food giant KFC KFC came to  check up I see 24 people went for the  job 23 people accepted I was not a guy  then Marv got a job at a local  university until English there for about  five years  earning just fifteen dollars a month on  the side he started a translation  company with several friends during a  company trip to the u.s. in 1995 ma had  his first encounter with the Internet at  a friend's place in Seattle I searched  the first award of beer I don't know if  it is easy to spell a baby and I see  beers from Germany beers from USA so he  searched for the word China instead and  still couldn't find anything and that  got him thinking he wanted to build  something that would put China on the  world's map he started China pages a  yellow pages like website but it didn't  take off then ma joined a government  agency in Beijing helped set up a  website by 1999 the internet stopped  boom had gripped Wall Street and back in  his hands yo apartment Marv decided to  try again with his wife and a group of  friends Marv raised $80,000 and set up  Alibaba  a site that allow businesses to sell  stuff to each other by 2000 Alibaba had  raised twenty five million dollars from  investors including Goldman Sachs and  Softbank  if you have no business plan and zero  revenue but his eyes was in 2003  Alibaba started Taobao a platform for  individual sellers to trade with each  other and publicly declared war against  eBay who had started to make a foray  into China  Chacma has this famous saying that  Alibaba is a crocodile in the Yangtze  River whereas eBay is a shark in the  ocean and if they fight eBay in the  ocean then they'll lose but if they  fight them in the Yangtze River then  they have a home base advantage  [Music]  in 2007 just one year after it force  eBay out of China  Alibaba debuted its business facing  division on the Hong Kong stock exchange  but it delisted five years later as its  performance sagged but in 2014  Alibaba raised 25 billion dollars in the  world's biggest IPO in New York  everybody should have a dream what if  that dream comes true after achieving  dominance in the business of e-commerce  in China Alibaba has been building an  Internet empire worth four hundred and  seventy two billion dollars with  businesses in cloud computing online  video streaming movie production  healthcare sports retail and even news  media although buying in to South China  Morning Post really raised eyebrows this  is the largest English newspaper in Hong  Kong and it shows that jack Moz  ambitions were limited to e-commerce he  wanted to influence not just Chinese  users but also overseas users as well  the u.s. is criticized Alibaba for  allowing companies to sell counterfeit  and poorly made goods but in China it  enjoys the favor of Chinese government  it's part of Mars company philosophy  they love with the government but don't  marry that we're done jack was an  extremely fortunate man for jumping on  the internet sector so early note that  this is a person who has no coding  skills at all he's a natural showman and  a gifted public speaker and really able  to convince others to believe in his  vision mass vision of growing Alibaba to  be the world's fifth largest economy  faces strong competition at home and  abroad it will require more than just  naked ambition in charisma but Maher is  great at getting himself in the right  place at the right time so far it's  well  you

